  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-05-04T18:29:04.476Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Came up with an idea while reading on people complaining about an unfair perma block.\nWhat if we have a timeout for a block.\nSame concept as most apps do now with the mute feature, you can mute for 30m, 1h, 24h, forever, etc.\nSo what if we have the same concept implemented with the block feature.\nThe main goal here is to have less harsh punishment over minor offences, but of course it's up to you what you consider minor.\nSo lets say when you click to block someone, you then presented with an option for how long you want that person to stay blocked: 30m, 1h, 24h, or forever\nLike for example you are in a public world, and lot of crazy stuff happening, but you are not sure that every one of the noisy people there is a crashed/nuisance, and you don't want to make the harsh decision of blocking them forever and preventing you from meeting them under better circumstances in the future. So having that feature rather allow you to block them temporary for only an hour. So that way you get your quiet now, and still leave the chance to see them in the future, up to you.",
